# requirements.v1 — append-only owner requirement rows

Put this file at `<product>/.hub/requirements.jsonl` (one JSON object per line).
Do not summarize away rows. Conflicts get a new row with `status: conflict` and `supersedes`.

```json
{"requirement_id":"REQ-001","verbatim_intent":"shortest faithful quote","status":"captured","ts":"2026-01-01T00:00:00Z"}
```

Statuses: `captured` | `planned` | `implemented` | `verified` | `blocked` | `explicitly_retired` | `conflict`

`state require --append` writes `requirement_id` / `verbatim_intent` / `status` / `ts`. Extra fields are optional notes.
